# --- Local development tooling. Not part of the deliverable. ----------------
# Agent configs, session scratch, and prompt files are how a given machine was
# driven, not what this project is. They stay local so the tree reads as the
# engineering artifact it is. The tracked tooling under scripts/ and
# .github/workflows/ is the opposite case: it is part of the deliverable and
# stays public.
.claude/
.mcp.json
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.cursorrules
.aider*
.continue/
.windsurfrules
.github/copilot-instructions.md
docs/superpowers/
# docs/design/ is tracked: it is the spec, and the spec is a deliverable.
scratchpad/
.scratchpad/
# Narrower than prompt*.md, which would also swallow a legitimate page such as
# docs/prompting.md.
/PROMPT.md
/PROMPTS.md
**/*-prompt.md
**/*_prompt.md
prompts/
.superpowers/
.agents/
_MAILBOX.md
scripts/hooks/prepare-commit-msg

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. An unanchored build/ or dist/ would
# also swallow a package directory that happens to carry that name.
/build/
/dist/
/sdist/

# --- uv ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.uv/
.uv-cache/

# --- Tool caches ------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ty_cache/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/

# --- Coverage ---------------------------------------------------------------
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# --- Rust -------------------------------------------------------------------
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# Cargo.lock is committed: the device agent ships as a binary, so the exact
# dependency set is part of what gets released.

# --- Node -------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/

# --- DuckDB -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.ddb
.duckdb_history

# --- Delta and local lakehouse artifacts ------------------------------------
# Scratch tables written by a local simulation run. A Delta table is a
# directory, so the local data root is ignored wholesale. A _delta_log under a
# tracked fixture table is deliberately NOT ignored: it is part of that table.
data/local/
lakehouse/local/
data/local/**/_delta_log/

# --- Docs build -------------------------------------------------------------
/site/
.cache/
sbom.cdx.json

# --- Secrets and local config -----------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!tests/**/*.key

# The IP-hygiene denylist holds client and employer names, so committing it to
# a public repository is the disclosure the scan exists to prevent. The example
# beside it is tracked and carries placeholders and the instructions.
.ip-denylist
!.ip-denylist.example

# --- IDE --------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Tool caches ------------------------------------------------------------
# import-linter memoises the import graph here. A stale entry reports every
# contract as KEPT over a tree that breaks them, which is why every recipe and
# workflow that runs it passes --no-cache. Committing the cache would spread
# that false green to everybody who cloned.
.import_linter_cache/

# --- OS junk ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
